                            <p class="span">In the modern visual digital era, images are not merely tools of design anymore. They are essential in the SEO ranking, performance of the website and the user experience. Images can be sourced to generate a lot of organic traffic through Google images when optimized in the right way, faster page loading speed and higher searches in general.</p> 
                            <p class="span">But <strong>Image SEO ranking factors</strong> have continued to be overlooked by many websites that assume Google is interested only in text. That's a big mistake.</p> 
                            <p class="span">You will be able to begin improving pictures optimization in this blog, and after that, we will dissect <strong>Image SEO ranking factors</strong> that really count one by one and explained step by step, so you will know how to begin improving image optimization the proper way.</p><br>                       
            
                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="1">Step 1: Select the correct Image file name (No random numbers)</h3>
                            <p class="span">Image file name is among the most ignored <strong>Image SEO ranking factors</strong>.</p>

                            <p class="span"><b>The majority of individuals post photos with such names as:</b></p>
                            <li>IMG_001.jpg</li>
                            <li>Screenshot123.png</li>
                            <li>Google does not comprehend such names.</li>
                            <p class="span">Rather, the name of your image file must be a description of what is in the image, in terms of relevant words.</p>

                            <p class="span"><b>Best Practices:</b></p>
                            <li>Use rich file names that are descriptive with the use of key words.</li>
                            <li>Hyphenated words Separated.</li>
                            <li>Don't use the use of special characters or underscore.</li><br>

                            <p class="span"><b>Example:</b></p>
                            <li>IMG_2456.jpg</li>
                            <li>image-seo-ranking-factors-guide.jpg</li>
                            <p class="span">This is a mere action that enables Google to know the contents of your image before even it loads.</p><br>

                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="2">Step 2: Maximize Alt Text (Alt Attributes) Ideally</h4>
                            <p class="span">One of the <strong>Image SEO ranking factors</strong> is the alt text optimization.</p>    
                            <p class="span"><b>Alt text:</b></p>
                            <li>Helps search engines are image cognizant.</li>
                            <li>Enhances accessibility among the visually impaired users.</li>
                            <li><strong>Appears when the pictures are not loaded.</strong></li><br>

                            <p class="span"><b>Alt text should be written in ways that are SEO friendly:</b></p>
                            <li>Clearly describe the image</li>
                            <li>Also add key words where appropriate.</li>
                            <li>Keep it under 125 characters</li>
                            <li>Avoid keyword stuffing</li><br>
                                 
                            <p class="span"><b>Example:</b></p>
                            <li>Image seo image seo image ranking</li>
                            <li>Image SEO ranking: A step-by-step guide.</li>
                            <p class="span">Google pays immense importance to alt attributes and therefore, never miss this step.</p><br> 
                                  
                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="3">Step 3: Choose the Right Image Format (JPEG, PNG, WebP)</h4>
                            <p class="span">The page speed is one of the established Google ranking factors that directly depend on the format of the images.</p> 

                            <p class="span"><b>Best Image Formats for SEO:</b></p>
                            <li>JPEG - Ideal with photos, not so large files.</li>
                            <li>PNG - Ideal when the logo has to be transparent or it is a logo.</li>
                            <li>WebP - Best (high quality and smaller size)</li>

                            <p class="span">WebP images can be very helpful in increasing the Core Web Vitals, particularly Largest Contentful Paint (LCP). When your site has WebP, then prioritise it so that it can perform better on Image SEO.</p><br> 

                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="4">Step 4: Reduce Image Size without compromise of the quality</h4>
                            <p class="span">Big picture images drag down your site. Slow websites rank poorly.</p> 
                            <p class="span">That is why one of the most important <strong>Image SEO ranking factors</strong> is image compression.</p> 

                            <p class="span"><b>Recommended Image Size:</b></p>
                            <li>Keep images under 100-150 KB</li>
                            <li>For banners, under 200 KB </li><br>

                            <p class="span"><b>Tools for Image Compression:</b></p>
                            <li>TinyPNG</li>
                            <li>ShortPixel</li>
                            <li>ImageOptim</li>
                            <li>Squoosh</li>
                            <p class="span">Smaller-sized images will load more quickly, will improve user experience, and will reduce the bouncing rates, and this will affect <a href="https://www.kingofdigitalmarketing.com/SEO-Services.aspx">SEO</a> positively.</p><br>

                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="5">Step 5: Ensure there are Mobile-Friendly and responsive images</h4>
                            <p class="span">Google applies mobile first indexing, which implies that it will assess your site by its performance in mobile first. In case your pictures cannot be responsive, your Image SEO ranking will be low.</p> 
                            <p class="span"><b>Best Practices:</b></p>
                            <li>Use responsive image sizing</li>
                            <li>Use srcset in varying sizes.</li>
                            <li>Avoid fixed-width images</li>
                            <li>Prejudice on different devices.</li>
                            <p class="span">Optimizing images to mobile will enhance interaction, lower the load time and boost the ranking of your pages by Google.</p><br> 

                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="6">Step 6: Embark on Positioning of Images in Content</h4>
                            <p class="span">Placing images influences the search engines to determine content relevancy.</p> 
                            <p class="span"><b>Smart Image Placement Tips:</b></p>
                            <li>Image proximity Place images next to matching text.</li>
                            <li>Add images after headings (H2/H3)</li>
                            <li>Support contextual keywords with the help of images.</li>
                            <li>Google links pictures with the text around them, and thus putting pictures in the right place reinforces your keywords.</li>
                            <p class="span">This has a direct influence on <strong>Image SEO ranking factors</strong> on content understanding.</p><br>

                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="7">Step 7: Image Structured Data (Schema Markup)</h4>
                            <p class="span">The structured data will assist Google to perceive pictures better and may enhance rich results.</p> 
                            <p class="span"><b>Image-Related Schema Types:</b></p>
                            <li>Article schema</li>
                            <li>Product schema</li>
                            <li>Recipe schema</li>
                            <li>Image Object schema</li><br>

                            <p class="span"><b>The image structured data will enhance the likelihood of:</b></p>
                            <li>The presence in Google Discover.</li>
                            <li>Showing in rich snippets</li>
                            <li>Increased presence in image search.</li>
                            <li>It is a more sophisticated yet effective Image SEO optimization.</li><br>

                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="8">Step 8: Incorporate images to XML Sitemap</h4>
                            <p class="span">Image sitemap assists search engines in locating images that would have remained unidentified.</p> 
                                
                            <p class="span"><b>Particularly, it is applicable to:</b></p>
                            <li>E-commerce websites</li>
                            <li>Portfolio websites</li>
                            <li>Image intensive blogs.</li>
                            <li>Benefits of Image Sitemap:</li>
                            <li>Faster image indexing</li>
                            <li>Better crawl efficiency</li>
                            <li>Greater presence in Google Image Search.</li>
                            <p class="span">Improving your technical Image SEO ranking factors by means of including images in your sitemap.</p><br> 

                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="9">Step 9: Optimize Image Context and Captions</h4>
                            <p class="span">Captions are normally neglected, however they are very conspicuous and are often read by people.</p>
                            <p class="span"><b>Although captions do not directly affect the rankings, they:</b></p>
                            <li>Improve user engagement</li>
                            <li>Increase time on page</li>
                            <li>Enhance the contextual relevance.</li>
                            <li>Natural captions with key words are not over optimized.</li>
                            <li>This indirectly helps User signals increase the ranking of Image SEO.</li><br>

                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="10">Step 10: Do not overuse Stock Imagery</h4>
                            <p class="span">Thousands of websites use the same pictures of stocks, which lowers originality.</p>
                            <p class="span">Google favors original and distinctive pictures.</p>
                            <p class="span"><b>Best Practices:</b></p>
                            <li>Use personal images as much as possible.</li>
                            <li>Watermark or add branding lightly.</li>
                            <li>Modify inventory pictures to create originality.</li>
                            <li>Original images enhance content authenticity, trust and search visibility.</li><br>

                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="11">Step 11: Lazy Load Image for optimization</h4>
                            <p class="span">Lazy loading is a delay that does not load images until it is required.</p>
                            <p class="span"><b>Benefits:</b></p>
                            <li>Faster initial page load</li>
                            <li>Improved Core Web Vitals</li>
                            <li>Better SEO performance</li>
                            <li>Apply loading lazy to below the fold images.</li>
                            <p class="span">This optimization allows being able to keep the speed and use high-quality visuals.</p><br>

                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="12">Concluding Ideas: Image SEO Is Not an Option anymore.</h4>
                            <p class="span">Image optimization is no longer a wish to have task in SEO. It's a core ranking strategy.</p>
                            <p class="span"><b>By prioritizing on Image SEO ranking factors which really count such as:</b></p>
                            <li>Alt text optimization</li>
                            <li>Image compression</li>
                            <li>Responsive design</li>
                            <li>Page speed</li>
                            <li>Structured data</li>
                            <p class="span">You will be able to increase your visibility, user experience, and organic traffic very much.</p>
                            <p class="span">Begin implementing these stepwise <strong>Image SEO methods</strong> and you will be enjoying the long term SEO benefits which most of your competitors are still neglecting.</p>

